{
  "adaptations": [
    "HIA number lexer and serde i64/u64/f64 classification, including -0 and overflow-to-f64.",
    "Pinned integer decimal-to-binary64 math receives a source span and returns private bits; no host floating-point or JSON runtime.",
    "Pinned shortest-binary64 formatter keeps its integer core and adopts actual zmij fixed exponent range -5..15 and non-padded exponent digits.",
    "Pinned UTF-8 decoder helpers are reused; generic Value uses 127-container admission, stable byte-key sort and final duplicate selection. Every numeric node is validated before duplicate selection.",
    "Arena and parser storage are relocated into disjoint workspace spans; complete measurement precedes output. Per-invocation previous numeric lexeme and exact 64-bit float text reuse retain invalid-value admission and signed-zero distinction.",
    "Owner/Legacy typed maps and arrays have separate direct parsing, duplicate-known bits and iterative IgnoredAny grammar; no generic Value precheck.",
    "HIA filter packer emits the original closed syscall transport with explicit 16/64/256 MiB buffers and no interpreter or libc."
  ],
